WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.853
The prize ceremony produces a clear picture of

00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:04.571
discovery,

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:08.028
with a handful of faces attached to a complicated

00:00:08.028 --> 00:00:09.369
scientific history.

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:17.205
Experiments accumulate through earlier questions,

00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:20.706
technical adaptations, overlooked collaborators and

00:00:20.706 --> 00:00:24.070
results that sometimes become useful years later.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.591
A manuscript records coauthors, while a method may

00:00:32.591 --> 00:00:33.006
depend

00:00:33.006 --> 00:00:36.466
on technicians, students and predecessor teams who

00:00:36.466 --> 00:00:36.812
never

00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:38.103
enter the headline.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.163
Every selection tells us whom an institution has

00:00:46.163 --> 00:00:46.599
chosen

00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:50.520
to remember. Historical recognition is never identical

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:50.665
to

00:00:50.665 --> 00:00:53.233
an exhaustive chain of contribution.

00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:01.880
An inclusive account cannot simply invent forgotten

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:05.511
heroes. It must return to papers, notebooks, patents

00:01:05.511 --> 00:01:05.720
and

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.503
who actually did the work.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.449
The essay asks for better histories of discovery

00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:15.945
without

00:01:15.945 --> 00:01:19.492
denying that major scientific contributions deserve

00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:20.327
recognition.
